+# Tool input validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+The registry enforces the schema advertised to providers before a tool executor receives input.
+
+## Contract
+
+- Invalid input returns a `ToolResponse` describing required properties, property paths and failed type or enum constraints without disclosing input values in results or logs; executors receive only accepted input, exactly once and unchanged, including unknown keys, with no coercion or defaults, while unknown tool names still throw `Unknown tool: <name>` ([validated by: rejects malformed calls privately and accepts corrected input unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L14)).
+- Static schemas compile at registration, reject uncompilable schemas with the tool name in the error, and reuse the compiled schema across ten executions without rereading it ([validated by: compiles static schemas at registration and reuses them for ten calls](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L82)).
+- Function-valued definitions resolve on each execution, compile the currently resolved schema, and reuse compilation by schema object identity when a previously resolved schema returns ([validated by: validates each dynamic schema and reuses previously resolved schema objects](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L120)).
+
+## Integration and migration
+
+A rejected call is a tool result for the next provider round, so the model can correct it within the existing five-round bound; it must not become a transport exception.
+The one-line `execute` doc comment points to this contract; unknown names retain their existing exception behavior and executor errors are not validation rejections.
+
+The implementation adds the JSON Schema validator as a runtime dependency and preserves the package build/import check.
+README.md, docs/adding-a-tool.md and .specify/spec.md must explain validation, unchanged extra keys and returned rejections.
+The changelog and MINOR release migration note explain that executors no longer receive malformed input for custom handling.
diff --git a/src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts b/src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts
